    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0560" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/877: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-25T18:00:00+03:25">October 25, 1943—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 26—12:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1019. The Medjliss, continuing its current wave of activity yesterday passed
                    following three bills: (1) law authorizing employment of 60 Americans (2) bill
                    ratifying the trade agreement (see my last one on trade treaty<anchor n="59"
                        xml:id="d573-f1"/>) and (3) bill authorizing employment of military mission.
                    I shall now press Foreign Office for signature of Ridley contract. Repeated to
                    Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d573-f1" n="59" xml:id="d573-f1-content">
                <p>Possibly telegram No. 960, September 27, 10 a.m., not printed.</p>
